content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-101, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22120, filtered-water line. Pumps P-101 to P-106 on this line are chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite [C16].",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Dry running: the applicable manual requirement is Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and 'never run dry'; no permissible dry-run duration is given. The reported approximately 15-minute dry run therefore breached that requirement. The pump is now reported primed and running.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: Figure 3 applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on the bearing housings. Numerically, the reported 3.0 mm/s lies in Zone B, 2.8-4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is above Zone A's 2.8 boundary, below Zone C at 4.5-7.1 ('Restricted - plan maintenance'), and below Zone D at 7.1-11.0 ('Damage likely - stop the pump'). The reported value is therefore not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone and does not trigger SSP-07's immediate-stop rule, subject to confirming the measurement method and location.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature: bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface, and the applicable limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reported 69 C is within the normal range, 1 C below its upper value, 11 C below alarm and 21 C below trip. Because it is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, SSP-07's requirement for a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered by this reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No shaft-seal leakage has been observed yet, so seal damage is not confirmed. P2 is assigned for prompt planned intervention because the dry-run prohibition was breached and seal run dry is a documented concern, while neither the reported vibration nor temperature presently requires an immediate stop or the temperature-related P1 response.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Primary concern: mechanical-seal damage resulting from the dry run. The troubleshooting table associates worn or cracked seal faces and 'seal run dry' with leakage at the shaft seal. Since no leakage is currently reported, treat this as the leading condition to inspect for rather than a confirmed failure.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional alternatives if abnormal readings develop: for high vibration, the manual lists misalignment, bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation; for high bearing temperature, it lists over-greasing, bearing wear and misalignment. These are not established causes at the currently reported 3.0 mm/s and 69 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Planned scope: carry out a controlled internal inspection and precautionary renewal of the dry-run-exposed mechanical seal, using the serial-specific seal bulletin. This is a planning decision, not a statement that seal failure has already been confirmed. Before isolation, verify and record vibration as mm/s RMS on the bearing housings and temperature on the bearing-housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the pump remains in service, keep it primed and do not allow further dry running. If vibration is confirmed in Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. If bearing temperature rises above the 80 C alarm limit, raise a P1 work order within the shift; the manual trip value is 90 C. Zone C vibration requires restricted operation and planned maintenance.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For internal or seal work, isolate and drain the pump. Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit, draining and venting first. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because this is a chemically dosed line.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Arrange a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment before removing the back pull-out assembly: its mass is 68 kg, exceeding SSP-07's 25 kg threshold, and the manual specifically requires lifting equipment. Remove the assembly using the back pull-out arrangement, which avoids disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the existing seal and sleeve. Inspect the seal faces for wear or cracking and inspect and record shaft-sleeve scoring. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit new pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B; do not fit HF3-450 on this serial. No sleeve-setting measurement is needed for the pre-set HF3-450B, but the sleeve-scoring inspection and replacement criterion still apply. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket with the seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten the fasteners as follows: casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm and impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm; if bearing-housing bolts are disturbed, tighten M12 bolts to 85 Nm. These Table 5 values are for lightly oiled threads. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm under SB-2026-014, not the manual's superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Alignment tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular offset 0.05 mm per 100 mm. If high vibration is verified, also inspect the bearings and impeller and check NPSH; if high bearing temperature develops, check grease quantity. Replace both bearings as a pair only when either shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, ensure the pump is primed and never run dry. Inspect for shaft-seal leakage and repeat the housing-surface temperature and bearing-housing RMS vibration checks. Apply the Zone D stop rule and above-alarm P1 rule; if leakage or abnormal readings are found, troubleshoot rather than simply returning the pump to normal operation.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal, quantity one for the planned seal replacement. Required in place of HF3-450 for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above; no sleeve-setting measurement is needed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Install new with the seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, conditional part: issue for replacement only if inspection shows scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3, conditional only. Do not add bearing replacement solely on the current readings; if bearing replacement is justified, replace this bearing together with HF3-510 as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3, conditional only. Replace together with HF3-512 when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves; and a line-break permit, with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the 68 kg back pull-out assembly: lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment. The component exceeds the procedure's 25 kg threshold, and the manual separately states that lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because P-101 is on the filtered-water line dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Operational controls: stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart if vibration reaches the manufacturer's highest severity zone; raise a P1 work order within the shift if bearing temperature exceeds the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Planned mechanical-seal replacement: standard allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: add 1.5 hours with 1 technician when required because the motor or bearing housing was moved.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement: add 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12 technician-hours, only if pair replacement is justified by wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part and gland torque: the manual parts table identifies component seal HF3-450, and Table 5 gives seal gland nuts a general torque of 25 Nm. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 and requires pre-set cartridge HF3-450B at 30 Nm for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-101 is serial HF3-22120, so the bulletin applies to this asset and supersedes those manual entries; the below-HF3-22000 exception does not apply. Continue using Table 5 for the other fastener torques.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve measurement versus inspection: the bulletin statement that HF3-450B needs no sleeve measurement applies to installation of the pre-set seal. It does not remove the manual requirement to inspect the withdrawn sleeve for scoring; HF3-455 must still be replaced if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "The evidence does not establish actual seal damage or explicitly mandate seal replacement after every dry run when no leakage is present. C09 gives seal replacement under leakage troubleshooting and C10 provides the procedure; confirm if site policy requires inspection-only, condition-based replacement instead of this order's precautionary renewal. [C09, C10]",
    "Confirm that the reported 3.0 mm/s was measured as RMS velocity on a bearing housing and that 69 C was measured on the bearing-housing surface. Otherwise, direct comparison with Figure 3 and the bearing-temperature limits is not fully established. [C01, C07]",
    "The actual sleeve condition and whether the dry run caused any bearing or impeller damage are unknown until inspection. The supplied evidence does not support adding further repair scope or parts now. [C09, C10, C13]",
    "What allowed the pump to run dry during tank changeover, and what operating, level-control or changeover change will prevent recurrence? The supplied chunks state that dry running is prohibited but do not explain the incident's root cause. [C02]",
    "SSP-07 specifies P1 timing for temperature above alarm but supplies no P2/P3 definitions or completion deadline. Confirm the required completion date for this P2 order; no post-restart inspection frequency or monitoring duration is supplied either. [C15]",
    "Table 6 provides no standalone standard time for inspection, isolation, lifting, or return-to-service checks; those allowances must not be inferred from the seal-replacement time. [C12]"
  ]
}
